%I A397921 #36 Aug 19 2026 21:58:39
%S A397921 1,3,77,125,16807,128807153,2357947691
%N A397921 Numbers k such that tau(k)*sigma(k)+1 is a multiple of k.
%C A397921 The results of the division are: 2,3,5,5,7,17,11... (is this related to A338141?) which are equivalent to the tau values of the numbers plus one (does this hold true for larger numbers?).
%C A397921 p^(p-2) (A130614) is a term for all primes p since tau(p^(p-2)) * sigma(p^(p-2)) + 1 = p^(p-1). - _Amiram Eldar_, Aug 13 2026
%e A397921 3 has divisor count 2 and sigma 4, and 4*2+1 = 9 is equal to 3 divided by 3.
%e A397921 77 has divisor count 4, and divisor sum 96 and 96*4+1 = 385 divided by 77 is 5.
%t A397921 q[k_] := Divisible[Times @@ DivisorSigma[{0, 1}, k] + 1, k]; Select[Range[20000], q] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Aug 13 2026 *)
%o A397921 (PARI) isok(k) = {my(f = factor(k)); !((numdiv(f)*sigma(f)+1)%k);} \\ _Amiram Eldar_, Aug 13 2026
%Y A397921 Cf. A000203, A000005, A064840, A130614.
%K A397921 nonn,more
%O A397921 1,2
